## Why This Is Asked

Tests resilience design when an external dependency degrades under load, forcing SREs to plan timeouts, circuit breakers, fallbacks, and SLO renegotiation rather than manual fixes.

## Key Concepts

- Timeout-based gating, circuit breakers (tripping thresholds and backoff)
- Fallback strategies and graceful degradation
- Caching and idempotence for safe retries
- SLI/SLI-based rollback and controlled rollouts
- Chaos testing in staging

## Code Example

```javascript
class CB {
  constructor(threshold=5, openMs=120000){
    this.fail=0; this.state='CLOSED'; this.openUntil=0;
  }
  call(p){
    if(this.state==='OPEN' && Date.now()<this.openUntil) throw new Error('Open');
    // call p()
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the circuit breaker in staging with load ramps?
- How to adjust SLO targets when external dependency quality changes?

